<title>USA: Arch Communications Q4 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Arch Communications Q4 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>WESTBOROUGH, Mass. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In 000s, except for share and per share data)</p>
<p>			  Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>				 Dec. 31,		 Dec. 31,</p>
<p>			  1996	  1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net revenues (a) $86,594     $57,755    $303,901    $141,809</p>
<p> Total EBITDA (b)  30,282	21,241     105,801	47,186</p>
<p> Margin (c)	   35.0%	 36.8%	 34.8%	 33.3%</p>
<p>Net income (loss) before</p>
<p>extraordinary charge</p>
<p>			(35,525)    (17,815)   (112,758)    (34,918)</p>
<p>Extraordinary charge from</p>
<p>early extinguishment</p>
<p>  of debt (d)	    --	    --	(1,904)     (1,684)</p>
<p>Accretion of redeemable</p>
<p>  preferred stock     (84)	 (102)	 (336)	 (102)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) to</p>
<p>common stockholders</p>
<p>			(35,609)    (17,917)   (114,998)    (36,704)</p>
<p>EBITDA per common share</p>
<p>			   1.47	  1.10	  5.17	  3.50</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share</p>
<p>before extraordinary</p>
<p>  charge (e)	  (1.72)	(0.92)	(5.53)	(2.60)</p>
<p>Extraordinary charge per share</p>
<p>			     --	    --	 (0.09)	(0.12)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per</p>
<p>  common share	(1.72)	(0.92)	(5.62)	(2.72)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>outstanding	 20,660,625  19,383,578  20,445,943  13,497,734</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Arch Communications Group Inc.</p>
<p>(a) Net revenues are service, rental and maintenance revenues, plus product sales, less cost of products sold.</p>
<p>(b) Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation and Amortization.</p>
<p>(c) Margin is EBITDA divided by net revenues.</p>
<p>(d) Extraordinary charge from early extinguishment of debt represented write-off of unamortized deferred financing costs for the prepayment of indebtedness under prior credit facilities.</p>
<p>(e) Net income (loss) to common stockholders less extraordinary charge from early extinguishment of debt divided by weighted average shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
